,vP:"1 day already measured here and left alone",w2:"1 day arrived out of order and was only used as context for the day that followed.",x8:"1 day folded into a shadow baseline. No day was added to any chart.",jw:"1 reading stored, each with the app that recorded it.",jo:"1 row arrived after its day had already been scored and closed.",Fk:": URI should have a non-empty host name: ",BA:"; straps do not read the same numbers as each other.",C:"A 7pm heads-up on any night with no wake alarm armed \u2014 silent otherwise",a:"A Colmi ring. Pairs and banks its history; nothing is decoded into a number yet.",d:"A Howear-branded band, paired through the WearFit app family.",L:"A Mi Band 2, 3 or 4. Pairs and connects; nothing derives from it yet.",J:"A Polar Verity Sense or OH1. Beat timing measured optically, streamed during a workout, same as a chest strap.",z4:"A band that has just come off the charger can take up to half a minute to start advertising.",sU:'A blank number stays blank. Only "What" is needed.',xi:"A briefing is written by a model you choose. Until you pick one there is nothing to generate and nothing has been sent anywhere.",qE:"A buzz on the strap and a notification on your phone through your waking hours, to remind you to log a drink. Nothing is measured either way",r:"A chest strap or armband, for beat timing during a workout.",z1:"A comparison, not a correction. Nothing on your readiness has been rescaled by this, and nothing here is a training instruction.",bd:"A cuff, a glucose meter, a thermometer. This band cannot measure any of them, which is the entire reason they are worth showing \u2014 and why the app that recorded each reading is named beside it.",bm:"A day counts once every occasion carries a figure and the log reaches the evening. None of the last ",xR:"A day counts once every occasion carries an energy figure.",y:"A device answers only while it is awake, worn, and not already connected to another phone or app.",dd:"A floor, not a rate for the day. Only stretches where you were almost completely still can be read at all, so these are the stillest few minutes the band saw outside your sleep \u2014 nothing here describes the rest of your day, and breathing while you move cannot be recovered from beat timing.",wx:"A heads-up about 45 minutes before the bedtime learned from your own nights, kept clear of your quiet hours. Appears after about a week of wear",la:"A heart-rate strap or a ring, alongside the band",k0:"A link on your own days \u2014 never a cause. The days you do a thing are days you were already that kind of day.",hi:"A long hold and a longer exhale. Usually used to get to sleep.",j7:"A nap is between 5 minutes and 6 hours. Anything longer is a sleep, and it belongs in the night where the stages can be read.",eT:"A ranking of three paces from one sitting. The blocks run back to back, so each pace is measured while you are still settling out of the one before. It says which pace your heart rate followed most strongly, and nothing else.",ou:"A removal is kept as a window rather than an id, so it still applies after the detector\u2019s edges move.",yu:"A scan sends the barcode to openfoodfacts.org, a free, open food database. They see the barcode and your IP address. Nothing about you, your meals or your health leaves this phone, and a barcode you have scanned before is answered from your own copy without asking them again.",Dc:"A screen, not a test.\n\nA day the screen did not fire is not a day you were cleared \u2014 it cannot rule anything out, and it never could. Outlined days were not screened at all: too few clean beats, or too much movement.\n\nWrist pulse is not an ECG. If symptoms are what brought you here, a clinician can test that properly.",jN:"A sensor answers a search only while it is awake, worn or damp, and not already connected to another phone or app.",lZ:"A sensor is used only while a workout is running, and only for heart rate and beat timing. It does not replace your band, it is never used overnight, and nothing it records feeds a score yet \u2014 its readings are stored and shown, and that is all.",I:"A sports watch. Reads battery and live heart rate \u2014 recorded activities stay on the watch.",hu:"ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789+/",sD:"Active energy from heart rate and your profile",r_:"Add a glass to today's water, same step as the + on the nutrition screen.",Ac:"Adds the Cycle tab to Wellness. Off hides it and keeps everything already logged",s:"All five thresholds are needed, lowest to highest. Nothing was saved.",y5:"An pulseAI backup (encrypted or not), a journal CSV you edited, a raw sensor export, or a vendor CSV. Days this band already measured are never overwritten",mJ:"Android only for events out. iOS can buzz the band but cannot be triggered by it",Bv:"Another sensor is using this phone\u2019s Bluetooth right now. Try pairing again in a moment.",bU:"Anything you want to remember about today",ET:"Ask about anything the app measures, and it can log food, water, workouts, doses and how you felt \u2014 always asking first.",wj:"Ask about efforts the band spotted that you did not start. Off hides the prompt and the review cards; the band goes on measuring either way",b6:"Asks openfoodfacts.org about the barcode, and fills in what it can stand behind",Dv:"Asks openstreetmap.org for the tiles covering this route. Off, the route draws on its own",iG:"At least one pace could not be scored, so there is nothing to rank. Nothing has changed.",C_:"Banister TRIMP over your waking heart rate, scaled to 0\u201321.",gx:"Banister training impulse \u2014 minutes weighted by heart-rate reserve. ",br:"Beat timing is stored and attributed to it during a workout. Nothing in the app is calculated from it yet.",te:"Breathe however you normally would. Nothing is pacing you and nothing is being scored.",C4:"Breaths per minute, recovered from beat timing",iW:"Briefings are generated on a schedule, or on demand here.",l